pat>      Options end up getting processed right to left.  The pickup without
pat> any value is treated as `autopickup,pickup_types:all' for backwards
pat> compatibility, thereby immediately replacing the `pickup_types:$' that
pat> you'd just set.

lars> Semantics like that will cause too much confusion.
lars> Why not just let pickup_types be "all" by default, rather than
lars> setting pickup_types implicitly when autopickup is set?
lars> It seems to me this would still provide full backward compatibility
lars> (to when pickup_types did not exist).

That is the case.  "autopickup" defaults to on and "pickup_types"
defaults to all types.

But for compatibility, when you set "pickup" (not "autopickup", and
not "pickup:$"), NetHack treats it as "autopickup,pickup_types:all",
which is what "pickup" meant before 3.1.2.


